## Natural Diamond Price Comparison: Pear vs Emerald Cut

At natural 1ct, certified market inventory shows pear cuts starting above emerald cuts at similar top grades. This surprises most buyers. The expectation is that brilliant cuts are always cheaper than step cuts because brilliant cuts require less rough to achieve good light performance.

Pear cuts command a shape premium that cushion cuts and oval cuts also carry — buyers pay for the silhouette.

At lower clarity grades (G-VS2, G-SI1), pear comes back into competitive territory. The practical question is what grade each shape actually needs to look good.

